WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.816
- [Man] This Great Big
Story was made possible

00:00:01.816 --> 00:00:03.270
by Wells Fargo,

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.924
established 1852, re-established 2018.

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:08.614
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:10.588
- [Narrator] Almost every
nationality on the planet

00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:12.239
is represented in the neighborhoods

00:00:12.239 --> 00:00:13.839
of Queens, New York,

00:00:13.839 --> 00:00:15.314
which means the streets are lined

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.344
with food from around the world.

00:00:17.344 --> 00:00:19.605
And if there's one man
who's tried them all,

00:00:19.605 --> 00:00:20.772
it's this guy.

00:00:21.742 --> 00:00:23.771
Don't be fooled by his slight frame.

00:00:23.771 --> 00:00:25.788
He spent the last 20 years unearthing

00:00:25.788 --> 00:00:29.538
every hidden gem this
side of the East River.

00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:36.123
- We're here in downtown Flushing,

00:00:36.123 --> 00:00:37.953
and there's all sorts of things here

00:00:37.953 --> 00:00:41.780
including Soy Bean Chen Flower Shop,

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.363
which is, of course, a florist.

00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:48.078
But you might wonder why
Soy Bean is in the name,

00:00:48.078 --> 00:00:50.775
and that's because they sell douhua,

00:00:50.775 --> 00:00:53.213
or fresh flower tofu,

00:00:53.213 --> 00:00:55.394
wonderful, warm, custardy tofu

00:00:55.394 --> 00:00:57.914
right out of this window.

00:00:57.914 --> 00:00:59.705
I love this one.

00:00:59.705 --> 00:01:00.797
What a great breakfast.

00:01:00.797 --> 00:01:03.214
(jazz music)

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.154
- Hi, Joe.

00:01:07.154 --> 00:01:08.674
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:01:08.674 --> 00:01:09.946
Cherry, my sister.

00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:10.779
How are you?

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.410
- It's good.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.930
- Pata Paplean specializes in Thai

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.207
boat noodles, and it's a really funky

00:01:18.207 --> 00:01:20.766
Thai bar with this crazy decor,

00:01:20.766 --> 00:01:22.683
and the owner's a trip.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.410
Where did you learn how
to make the boat noodles?

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.797
- I used to cook with my mom

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:31.549
when I was in Thailand
before I moved to New York.

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:34.319
And then, no other place
that make it in New York.

00:01:34.319 --> 00:01:35.152
- Aha.

00:01:35.152 --> 00:01:36.490
So it was out of necessity
- That's why I--

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.269
Yeah, that's why I try to make it in here.

00:01:39.269 --> 00:01:41.686
(jazz music)

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:53.693
- One of my favorite Tibetan restaurants,

00:01:53.693 --> 00:01:58.640
Lhasa Fast Food, is nestled
in-between You and Me Wireless

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.577
and Little Myanmar Mini Mart,

00:02:01.577 --> 00:02:06.204
one of the best places
for Tibetan Beef Momos.

00:02:06.204 --> 00:02:07.494
If you think you're lost on the way in,

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.094
just look for the prayer flags.

00:02:10.094 --> 00:02:12.885
(relaxing music)

00:02:12.885 --> 00:02:14.674
What makes the Moma unique is the masala,

00:02:14.674 --> 00:02:15.996
or seasoning, that's in there.

00:02:15.996 --> 00:02:19.934
So you find Sichuan
peppercorn, ginger, celery,

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.073
onion. I like to think of them as

00:02:22.073 --> 00:02:23.593
the hamburgers of the Himalayas,

00:02:23.593 --> 00:02:25.740
and I mean that as a compliment.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.490
(relaxing music)

00:02:29.341 --> 00:02:31.351
The reason that places like this resonate

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.513
with me is because

00:02:33.513 --> 00:02:36.641
they're not trying to
make it the next it thing,

00:02:36.641 --> 00:02:38.193
the next Instagram food.

00:02:38.193 --> 00:02:39.026
It's just like,

00:02:39.026 --> 00:02:41.094
"Hey, this is what we make back home.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.761
If you like it, too, come on in."

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:46.414
Queens has everything.

00:02:46.414 --> 00:02:47.886
Go explore the neighborhood

00:02:47.886 --> 00:02:49.366
and find what's out there.

00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:52.516
It's super easy, accessible, delicious,

00:02:52.516 --> 00:02:54.406
and people are a lot more welcoming

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.906
and open than you might think.

